  "principle": "Standard published practice: rapid mixing of coagulant (alum, ferric, PAC) destabilises colloids; slow flocculation builds settleable flocs; precipitation reagents (lime, caustic, metal sulphide) convert dissolved phosphate, metals and fluoride to insoluble solids removed by clarification; pH trim finishes the train.",
